index 4444da16163..0cf3654fa21 100644
--- a/release/src/router/www/BR.dict
+++ b/release/src/router/www/BR.dict
@@ -6685,3 +6685,44 @@ RDEV_90=The file contains real device names, MAC and IP addresses. Keep it somew
 RTRF_75=Upload only
 RTRF_76=The QoS engine classifies and shapes the upload direction only, so download traffic never reaches these queues and does not appear in this chart.
 RFW_252=Both
+RABT_00=About
+RABT_01=Hardened Asuswrt-Merlin - RT-BE Series
+RABT_02=A security-hardened, de-clouded rebuild of Asuswrt-Merlin for the ASUS RT-BE series. Compiled in a public clean room from a pinned upstream base and an open patch series, so the firmware on your router can be rebuilt, byte for byte, by anyone who doubts it - including you.
+RABT_03=Published by
+RABT_04=Version
+RABT_05=Base
+RABT_06=Model
+RABT_07=Variant
+RABT_08=Where this build came from
+RABT_09=Every release is compiled by a public GitHub Actions run, from public inputs only. Nothing is ever uploaded from a developer's machine. The figures below describe the image you are running right now.
+RABT_10=Patches applied
+RABT_11=Upstream base pin
+RABT_12=Built
+RABT_13=Build environment
+RABT_14=Clean room
+RABT_15=The people who made this
+RABT_16=Reaper is a set of patches. Everything underneath it, and most of what is good about it, came from other people - many of whom owed this project nothing at all.
+RABT_17=Creator and maintainer of Asuswrt-Merlin, the firmware every line of this build is patched on top of. Reaper is a fork with opinions; this is the thing it has opinions about. Remove him from the picture and there is no picture.
+RABT_18=Compile-integrity guidance, and a bug hunter with a genuinely unsettling hit rate. If a build was going to fall over, he tended to know before the build did.
+RABT_19=The QA department nobody hired, nobody budgeted for, and nobody can now imagine shipping a release without.
+RABT_20=Brought real operational experience to the reporting thread and quietly filtered the noise out of it. Half the value of a bug report is knowing it is a bug.
+RABT_21=Speaks quietly and infrequently. Every single time, it was worth stopping what I was doing to read it.
+RABT_22=Never once let a test build go untested. GT-BE98 owners have working firmware because these two kept flashing it and saying what happened.
+RABT_23=Sole, tireless and remarkably patient ambassador for the RT-BE88U. That model is in far better shape for it.
+RABT_24=Every tester, every screenshot, every "mine does that too". More than one release exists purely because somebody took the time to describe exactly what broke and when - which is a harder and rarer skill than it sounds.
+RABT_25=Genuinely excellent hardware, and plenty of it - a real pleasure to build on. The offer stands, by the way: let's talk global Reaper distribution. You bring the production line, I'll bring the patch series.
+RABT_26=Making wireless great again, one closed-source blob at a time. The silicon is superb and we would love to see more of the source, but we will take the wins we are given.
+RABT_27=Project
+RABT_28=source, patches & releases
+RABT_29=don't take our word for it -- rebuild it
+RABT_30=Everyone at SNBForums
+RABT_31=discussion & support
+RABT_32=Pay it forward
+RABT_33=Reaper is free and it stays free. No telemetry, no account, no cloud service behind it, nothing to unlock and nothing to buy. If it has earned its place on your router and you are in a position to, a contribution goes straight into test hardware and the hours behind each release. Please do not feel any obligation - a well-written bug report genuinely is worth as much, and costs you less.
+RABT_34=Donate
+RABT_35=Licence.
+RABT_36=Reaper is distributed under the GNU General Public License v2, as is the Asuswrt-Merlin base it builds on. The complete corresponding source for every release is published as a patch series against a pinned upstream commit - see the repository and the source-availability notes shipped alongside it.
+RABT_37=Vendor components.
+RABT_38=This firmware includes proprietary components supplied by ASUS and Broadcom, redistributed unmodified under their own terms. They are not covered by the GPL grant above.
+RABT_39=No warranty.
+RABT_40=Provided as-is, with no warranty of any kind. Reaper is an independent project and is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or supported by ASUS or Broadcom. Installing third-party firmware is done at your own risk and may void your warranty.
